    h1: "Can Title 24 and MEP Engineering Come from the Same Company?",
    answer: "Yes. No California rule requires separate providers for Title 24 compliance and MEP engineering, and using one company for both is common. It is often better, because the energy model and the mechanical, electrical, and plumbing design stay coordinated through every revision. The compliance documentation must still be independently checkable — plan checkers review the forms and the design on their own merits regardless of who prepared them.\n\nTitle 24 compliance is a claim about a specific design: these assemblies, this equipment, these controls, these schedules. MEP design is the ongoing evolution of that same design. Every time the two diverge — a substituted rooftop unit, a revised lighting control sequence, a value-engineered glazing change — the compliance documents drift from reality. One team holding both scopes closes that gap by construction, because the person updating the drawings sits next to the person updating the model.",
